# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
R1 VISUM STEP 11d v1.3
Component-level IDP DIST behavior baseline with current V5 IDP authority.

READ-ONLY SCRIPT. It does not modify the open Visum model.

Purpose
-------
This step closes the IDP probing phase and creates the first reproducible
model-side baseline diagnostics for the current R1/AMDY-like native vehicle
matrices:

1) Verify the inactive TFlowFuzzy scaffold produced by 11c v2.3:
   - Demand matrix correction operation type 66
   - ProcedureVariant readback TFLOWFUZZY
   - operation inactive

2) Recompute current traffic-count diagnostics from the live assignment:
   - passenger count model = NATIVE_* + EXOG_EE_*
   - freight LNV/NV is exported as a diagnostic column only
   - GEH is scored against R1_OBS_RPDI on CALIBRATION CountLocations
   - no matrix correction and no assignment are run

3) Read the fixed R1_OSRM_DIST_KM matrix and compare current mutable native
   vehicle demand against the locked IDP distance authority:
   - backend/guardrail metric: DIST_KM only
   - TIME_MIN is diagnostic only and is not a TFlowFuzzy backend constraint

4) Build atomic component-level IDP diagnostics for person matrices:
   - WORK_* components -> their own DIST_KM curves
   - SERV_* components -> their own DIST_KM curves
   - SCHOOL -> its own DIST_KM curve
   - LONG_* -> 100-200 km basis pending/freeze review
   - FOREIGN -> no domestic IDP target

5) Retain family-level composites only as assignment-family guardrails, not as
   final b,c calibration authority

5) Export a first LONG 100-200 km basis-mixture fit candidate against the
   current NATIVE_CL baseline.  This only proposes a reproducible set of basis
   weights for review; it is not written to Visum and is not frozen here.

This script intentionally does not bind TFlowFuzzy parameters and does not run
TFlowFuzzy.  A later step can use these diagnostics to decide whether to bind
counts + DIST_KM distribution constraints and/or prepare a bounded b,c candidate.

Required local authority files
------------------------------
The package contains R1_IDP_DISTRIBUTION_AUTHORITY_V1/*.csv.  Keep the folder
next to this script, or set R1_IDP_AUTHORITY_DIR to its path.  Version 1.3 also
contains an embedded compressed copy of the IDP authority and will auto-extract
it next to the script if the folder is missing.

Expected Visum state
--------------------
- current model already contains 11c v2.3 inactive TFlowFuzzy scaffold
- R1_OSRM_DIST_KM matrix exists (created/reused by 11c v2.2)
- current assignment volumes are available on links
- native matrices 9301..9306 and component person matrices 9101..9117 exist

The script DOES NOT save the .ver file automatically.
"""

